  era: "Section 20 \xB7 East India Company Rule \xB7 1765 \u2013 1858"
  title: Courts and law
  text: Warren Hastings set up civil and criminal courts in districts, and Cornwallis separated judicial and revenue work. The Supreme Court at Calcutta, in 1774, and later the High Courts, in 1862, applied codified laws such as the Indian Penal Code of 1860.
